| `check_pulse_request_nothing.sh` | When a HUNG_PULSE request's god answers NOTHING, or is anathema/forsaken with rawFavour >= 0, is the request removed rather than left pending? Before the fix either case stayed pending forever, so the SAME god won the lottery's request-first slot on every later poll and no other god -- not even one owed anger pulses -- was ever drawn again. Two runs, two scratch modules: run 1's patron always answers `NOTHING`; run 2's patron forsakes itself (`Expel`, no `EXP_CAST_OFF`) with favour kept >= 0. Both share a second, non-patron god owed anger pulses (`GS_INVOLVED`, raw favour -70000). Each follower rests once to file the request, then waits. The deciding assertion, each run: the patron's `refused` probe lines number at least 1 and at most its `stored=1` request lines (fixed code refuses each request once; the defect refuses on every poll). The angry god's pulse count is informational only, because the lottery's 25% non-patron draw is diluted across about eight involved gods (inc-pu6v.303). `--prove-red` reverts run 1's removal (exit (a)); moving the second `check_mutation` call above the first and re-running proves run 2's removal (exit (b)) the same way (inc-pu6v.54). | LIVE |
| `check_pulse_request_queue.sh` | When a follower raises two different pulse requests for one god before its next pulse, do both reasons reach the god? A scratch god raises `GPR_IDENTIFY` and `GPR_REST` together when the follower joins. The pulse probe log must show both requests stored before any pulse, then each reason delivered on its own scheduled pulse, and the handler must print both messages. Before the fix the second request overwrote the first. A mutation that makes each pulse remove every entry for the god turns it red (inc-pu6v.76). | LIVE |
| `check_pulse_status_length.sh` | Does a timed status a god's pulse gives last its full length? The pulse used to fire inside the follower's own turn, before that tick's status countdown, so a 2-unit status lasted 60 ticks, not 120. A scratch god (`tools/fixtures/pulse-status-god.irh`) pulses every 8 rounds and gives STUNNED for 2 units and CONFUSED for 3, to a loaded fixture character who dumps the screen after each wait. Each status MUST be on at every dump before its end minus the dump gap (about 16 ticks) and off at every dump after its end plus the gap; the pulse tick comes from the pulse probe log. Exit 2 when fewer than 2 pulses or statuses can be measured. `INCURSION_BIN=<unfixed binary>` shows it red (inc-pu6v.345). | LIVE |
| `check_punishment_mark.sh` | Do the command powers and Song of the Deep Stone refuse a creature a god sent as punishment (stati `GOD_PUNISHMENT`), with the approved line, while both still work on an unmarked creature? `INCURSION_PUNISH_MARK` marks one summoned earth elemental and `INCURSION_COMMAND_ROLL` fixes the command's d20. `tools/prove_punishment_mark.sh` removes each refusal in turn and shows it red (inc-pu6v.308). | LIVE |
